From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:37:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: join 2.4 GHz channels at 20 MHz

Admit 2.4 GHz channels in the join. The channel request and the BSS
record carry the band, and the BSS and station records carry the ERP PHY
type, with HR/DSSS unless the basic rates are OFDM, as the vendor sets
them. The CCK rates take their own positions in the firmware's rate set,
and short slot time follows the access point's capability. The band is
advertised with HT at 20 MHz, and frames are delivered with the join's
band.

Every frame's fixed rate is OFDM 6 Mbit/s, so a network without that rate
is refused. ERP protection stays off, which may matter beside 802.11b
stations.

mac80211 calls config only when the channel changes, and channel 1 is its
default. Stop clearing the channel's validity at a re-arm, so that a
second join on channel 1 is not refused. Accept an association request
whose HT element lacks the 40 MHz bit, since mac80211 clears it where the
channel does not allow 40 MHz.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 3.
